    {
      "text": "AN AVERAGING PROCESS FOR UNIPOTENT GROUP ACTIONS — We present an averaging process for sections of a torsor under a unipotent group.\n\n**AN AVERAGING PROCESS FOR UNIPOTENT GROUP ACTIONS**\n\n*AMNON YEKUTIELI*\n\n11 pp, 5 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We present an averaging process for sections of a torsor under a unipotent group. This process allows one to integrate local sections of such a torsor into a global simplicial section. The results of this paper have applica- tions to deformation quantization of algebraic varieties. 0. Introduction Let K be a ﬁeld of characteristic 0. For any natural number q let K[t0, . . . , tq] be the polynomial algebra, and let ∆q K be the geometric q-dimensional simplex ∆q K := Spec K[t0, . . . , tq]/(t0 + · · · + tq −1). Our main result is the following theorem. Theorem 0.1. Let G be a unipotent algebraic group over K, let X be a K-scheme, let Z be a G-torsor over X, and let Y be any X-scheme. Suppose f = (f0, . . . , fq) is a sequence of X-morphisms fi : Y →Z.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 0 Introduction; 1 The Averaging Process; 2 Simplicial Sections; References",
